{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1550942-recreating-the-elder-vampire-from-sinners-in-requiem","id":1550942,"title":"Recreating the Elder Vampire from Sinners in Requiem","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-05-11T10:23:02-07:00","id":1550942,"title":"Recreating the Elder Vampire from Sinners in Requiem","content":"Hi everyone !<br /> <br /> Just got out of Sinners and I loved the depiction of the Vampire in there. I'd love to have a version of him for my Chronicles, but I was wondering how to do that.<br /> <br /> I thought about using an Elder Gangrel with some Coils and Scales of the Dragons. Here's my reasoning :<br /> <br /> The Vampire is clearly old, as he states that he was forced to convert to Christianity so he's a White dude from Pagans lands.<br /> <br /> He would fit well with the Gangrels as he can have claws like hands and is hella resistant. <br /> <br /> Finally he seems to have some solar resistance first seen where he's seen is in the dusk) and even his abilities to &quot;mind-read&quot; his &quot;hive-mind&quot; could be a Coil ro Scale, I guess.<br /> <br /> Does it seems fitting to you, and what advices would you give for this dude ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-08T19:10:22-08:00","id":1557393,"title":"","content":"He's totally a Gangrel with dots in performance: he's not a Toreador from Masquerade; Remmick, isn't that old; he recited the Lord's prayer, in English, not Latin. He's probably Medieval. And bullets, definitely do bashing, that's for sure. It's got a high-level of Fortitude to withstand the Sun like that. He's got Auspex to mind-read, and lots of Dominate, maybe good Presence. He may think he was a Celtic-Bard, but, he's probably got the Fog of Eternity going. <br /> <br /> Now Sammy, the musician, he's definitely got a supernatural-merit going; maybe he's Second-Sight Sorcerer with a magical-merit for singing. I wouldn't say he was Cult of Estacy; he's not Enlightened in the sense a mage is. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T18:55:28-08:00","id":1557492,"title":"","content":"I just saw the movie. I might argue that Sammy's whole musical performance that bridges the eras could have been a sort of Mystery Play-style Awakening. He could easily be something like an Acanthus or possibly Mastigos. Then again, a one-off with Second Sight or some kind of hedge magic is also cool. <br /> <br /> Remmick as a Gangrel is a cool thing. I think that fits. He's not crazy in terms of stats, but torpor could have reduced some. His Humanity is not as low as it could be, which is why he's able to survive dusk. Keep in mind that his stats don't have to be particularly high, and for him, Embracing seems easier than for most Kindred. They're only dealing with mortals, and only a relatively tame amount of small arms. So they don't need to be any more than starting vampires to get it done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T00:18:38-08:00","id":1557581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1550942-recreating-the-elder-vampire-from-sinners-in-requiem?p=1557393#post1557393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remmick, isn't that old; he recited the Lord's prayer, in English, not Latin. </div> </div> </div> </div>He probably does that for the sake of going along with Sammy rather than authenticity to whatever language he originally spoke.<br /> <br /> Like, the dude can speak Mandarin from the moment he brings a native speaker into his club, his languages wouldn't be a great metric even if it wasn't explicit that he'd been hiding out in America for a long time or outright said that he's old enough to remember Christianity coming to Ireland.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T10:24:57-08:00","id":1557605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1550942-recreating-the-elder-vampire-from-sinners-in-requiem?p=1557581#post1557581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He probably does that for the sake of going along with Sammy rather than authenticity to whatever language he originally spoke.<br /> <br /> Like, the dude can speak Mandarin from the moment he brings a native speaker into his club, his languages wouldn't be a great metric even if it wasn't explicit that he'd been hiding out in America for a long time or outright said that he's old enough to remember Christianity coming to Ireland.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Elders, much like any other vampire or person in CoD's world in fact, can forget or misremember things, embelish or straight out lie about their pasts or have elements of their memories tampered with without noticing until the parts responsible are long gone or destroyed. What's the measure of a narrator's reliability?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T19:07:01-08:00","id":1557818,"title":"","content":"And when watching, was anyone else thinking about <i>Leperchaun in the Hood</i> (part 2)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1550942-recreating-the-elder-vampire-from-sinners-in-requiem?p=1557581#post1557581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He probably does that for the sake of going along with Sammy rather than authenticity to whatever language he originally spoke.<br /> <br /> Like, the dude can speak Mandarin from the moment he brings a native speaker into his club, his languages wouldn't be a great metric even if it wasn't explicit that he'd been hiding out in America for a long time or outright said that he's old enough to remember Christianity coming to Ireland.</div> </div> </div> </div>True; but his Irish-dancing, was from, furthest back the 17th-century or so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1550942-recreating-the-elder-vampire-from-sinners-in-requiem?p=1557605#post1557605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed. Elders, much like any other vampire or person in CoD's world in fact, can forget or misremember things, embelish or straight out lie about their pasts or have elements of their memories tampered with without noticing until the parts responsible are long gone or destroyed. What's the measure of a narrator's reliability?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's straight out of <i>Ancient Mysteries </i>stuff about the Fog of Eternity. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-24T12:56:25-08:00","id":1557880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/